1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,341
Welcome to the Employee three sixty data quality walkthrough, prepared

2
00:00:04,341 --> 00:00:08,682
for Anthony Grant Apollis. This presentation explains the supplied data,

3
00:00:08,682 --> 00:00:13,024
the release decision, the reconciliation findings, and the evidence included

4
00:00:13,024 --> 00:00:14,326
in the submission.

5
00:00:14,326 --> 00:00:18,216
The project compares three extracts: human resources, payroll, and the

6
00:00:18,216 --> 00:00:22,106
delivered Employee three sixty dataset. Each file contains forty eight

7
00:00:22,106 --> 00:00:25,996
rows. Equal row counts are only a starting point, because

8
00:00:25,996 --> 00:00:29,887
a missing employee and an unexpected employee can cancel each

9
00:00:29,887 --> 00:00:31,832
other out in the totals.

10
00:00:31,832 --> 00:00:36,308
The solution combines profiling, explicit quality rules, field comparisons, monitoring,

11
00:00:36,308 --> 00:00:40,784
and an incremental loading demonstration. The objective is to make

12
00:00:40,784 --> 00:00:45,260
defects explainable and traceable before the data is released for

13
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:45,707
reporting.

14
00:00:45,707 --> 00:00:49,631
This video uses the corrected presentation and recorded dashboard evidence.

15
00:00:49,631 --> 00:00:53,555
The narrator is computer generated. It is a slide based

16
00:00:53,555 --> 00:00:57,478
explanation, not a live screen recording or a clone of

17
00:00:57,478 --> 00:01:01,402
Anthony's voice. The accompanying code and evidence allow a reviewer

18
00:01:01,402 --> 00:01:02,972
to inspect the implementation.

19
00:01:02,972 --> 00:01:06,848
The release decision is block. That is a business control

20
00:01:06,848 --> 00:01:10,724
outcome: the checks have identified problems that require investigation. It

21
00:01:10,724 --> 00:01:14,600
does not mean the pipeline crashed, or that every employee

22
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:15,762
failed every check.

23
00:01:15,762 --> 00:01:19,798
The corrected local validation returns seventeen rule findings across twelve

24
00:01:19,798 --> 00:01:23,833
employee identifiers. All ten controls detect at least one defect.

25
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:27,868
Findings can overlap: one employee may violate several rules, and

26
00:01:27,868 --> 00:01:31,904
a stale record can appear in more than one source.

27
00:01:31,904 --> 00:01:35,583
A final review found a status mapping error in the

28
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:39,263
local implementation. A terminated employee with payroll marked Stopped is

29
00:01:39,263 --> 00:01:42,943
a consistent pair. The checker previously expected a different label

30
00:01:42,943 --> 00:01:46,623
and incorrectly flagged two valid pairs. That error has been

31
00:01:46,623 --> 00:01:49,935
corrected and a regression test now protects the mapping.

32
00:01:49,935 --> 00:01:54,163
These local output rows must be read separately from the

33
00:01:54,163 --> 00:01:58,391
historical Databricks lifecycle figures shown later. The implementations do not

34
00:01:58,391 --> 00:02:02,619
have identical rule identifiers or aggregation. The package records that

35
00:02:02,619 --> 00:02:05,579
limitation rather than claiming complete result parity.

36
00:02:05,579 --> 00:02:10,790
The assessment spans seven dimensions: uniqueness, completeness, referential integrity, consistency,

37
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:16,001
validity, timeliness, and reconciliation. Ten controls cover these dimensions, with

38
00:02:16,001 --> 00:02:21,212
a severity and a release action attached to each result.

39
00:02:21,212 --> 00:02:26,198
SQL is useful for readable profiling, joins, grouped checks, and

40
00:02:26,198 --> 00:02:31,184
dashboard queries. PySpark supports the distributed Databricks pipeline. The package

41
00:02:31,184 --> 00:02:36,170
also includes a local Python implementation for repeatable validation without

42
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:38,164
requiring a cloud workspace.

43
00:02:38,164 --> 00:02:41,914
One important business insight is that totals hide offsetting differences.

44
00:02:41,914 --> 00:02:45,663
The documented salary comparison shows a net difference of sixty

45
00:02:45,663 --> 00:02:49,413
four thousand six hundred rand, but a gross absolute difference

46
00:02:49,413 --> 00:02:53,163
of two hundred and twenty five thousand two hundred rand.

47
00:02:53,163 --> 00:02:57,415
The net amount allows overstatements and understatements to cancel. The

48
00:02:57,415 --> 00:03:01,667
gross amount sums their magnitudes and exposes a larger reconciliation

49
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:05,919
problem. Neither number is automatically a proven financial loss. Currency

50
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:10,172
conflicts and unverifiable payroll values must be investigated before the

51
00:03:10,172 --> 00:03:13,573
figures are used for payment or reporting decisions.

52
00:03:13,573 --> 00:03:17,862
The source comparison joins employee records on employee identifier. Payroll

53
00:03:17,862 --> 00:03:22,150
also has a pay period, so a comparison must select

54
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:26,438
the relevant period before joining. Otherwise multiple payroll rows could

55
00:03:26,438 --> 00:03:29,440
multiply the comparison and create misleading results.

56
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:33,376
Employee E one zero two seven exists upstream but is

57
00:03:33,376 --> 00:03:37,312
missing downstream. Employee E one zero nine nine appears downstream

58
00:03:37,312 --> 00:03:41,248
without the expected source employee. Its match to E one

59
00:03:41,248 --> 00:03:45,184
zero two eight across eight tested attributes supports a copied

60
00:03:45,184 --> 00:03:49,121
record hypothesis. Confirming the exact upstream cause requires source system

61
00:03:49,121 --> 00:03:49,514
lineage.

62
00:03:49,514 --> 00:03:53,887
The historical dashboard identifies six employees with field errors, covering

63
00:03:53,887 --> 00:03:58,259
attributes such as employment status, salary, currency, and other profile

64
00:03:58,259 --> 00:04:02,632
details. Employee E one zero one five has conflicting payroll

65
00:04:02,632 --> 00:04:07,004
values, so the outcome remains Cannot verify. Selecting an arbitrary

66
00:04:07,004 --> 00:04:09,191
value would hide the conflict.

67
00:04:09,191 --> 00:04:12,939
Employee E one zero four two is a documented future

68
00:04:12,939 --> 00:04:16,688
dated HR exception. That difference is displayed for transparency and

69
00:04:16,688 --> 00:04:20,437
excluded from failure counts. The local checker has narrower field

70
00:04:20,437 --> 00:04:24,185
coverage than the historical dashboard; the packaged scope note explains

71
00:04:24,185 --> 00:04:27,559
why those results should not be treated as interchangeable.

72
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:31,647
The three run demonstration tests change handling. Run one loads

73
00:04:31,647 --> 00:04:35,735
the supplied files. In the historical dashboard it starts with

74
00:04:35,735 --> 00:04:39,822
seventeen open lifecycle issues. That count describes the dashboard's issue

75
00:04:39,822 --> 00:04:43,501
model, not the row count of every packaged output.

76
00:04:43,501 --> 00:04:47,318
Run two presents the same files again. Matching file hashes

77
00:04:47,318 --> 00:04:51,134
allow the loader to skip an unchanged delivery, avoiding duplicate

78
00:04:51,134 --> 00:04:54,951
processing. An unchanged delivery does not resolve existing issues; they

79
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:58,768
remain open until later evidence shows the problem has gone

80
00:04:58,768 --> 00:04:59,149
away.

81
00:04:59,149 --> 00:05:03,703
Run three uses a separate, deliberately simulated delivery. It resolves

82
00:05:03,703 --> 00:05:08,257
eight earlier issues, introduces two new issues, and leaves eleven

83
00:05:08,257 --> 00:05:12,811
open. The arithmetic is seventeen, minus eight, plus two, which

84
00:05:12,811 --> 00:05:13,722
equals eleven.

85
00:05:13,722 --> 00:05:17,599
Resolved means a later evaluated delivery no longer triggers that

86
00:05:17,599 --> 00:05:21,476
issue. It does not mean the original supplied files were

87
00:05:21,476 --> 00:05:25,353
repaired. The simulation proves that the lifecycle responds to changes.

88
00:05:25,353 --> 00:05:29,230
The local regression test independently verifies file hash changes and

89
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:33,107
unchanged file skips; it does not claim to test streaming

90
00:05:33,107 --> 00:05:34,270
change data capture.

91
00:05:34,270 --> 00:05:38,525
The dashboard brings together the release decision, rule outcomes, affected

92
00:05:38,525 --> 00:05:42,781
employees, severity, and actions. Investigators can begin with a failing

93
00:05:42,781 --> 00:05:47,036
rule, identify the affected employee and source, and then inspect

94
00:05:47,036 --> 00:05:48,738
the record level evidence.

95
00:05:48,738 --> 00:05:52,373
Severity and release action are separate fields. A rule may

96
00:05:52,373 --> 00:05:56,008
block release, require an immediate alert, or remain under monitoring.

97
00:05:56,008 --> 00:05:59,643
Review the configured action for the rule rather than assuming

98
00:05:59,643 --> 00:06:03,277
every critical or high severity result has the same response.

99
00:06:03,277 --> 00:06:07,347
A technical failure is different. The earlier unsupported SQL subquery

100
00:06:07,347 --> 00:06:11,416
was an execution error, requiring an engineering fix. A successful

101
00:06:11,416 --> 00:06:15,486
job that reports failed data quality checks has completed its

102
00:06:15,486 --> 00:06:19,148
technical work and correctly exposed a business data problem.

103
00:06:19,148 --> 00:06:23,207
For a failed run, inspect the run identifier, failed task,

104
00:06:23,207 --> 00:06:27,266
error message, input delivery, and last successful stage. For a

105
00:06:27,266 --> 00:06:31,325
data defect, follow the employee, source, and rule to the

106
00:06:31,325 --> 00:06:35,383
responsible data owner. Retry after an operational repair; release only

107
00:06:35,383 --> 00:06:38,630
after the relevant quality controls have been satisfied.

108
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:43,002
The design separates raw ingestion, conformed data, and reporting outputs

109
00:06:43,002 --> 00:06:47,374
through Bronze, Silver, and Gold layers. Run identifiers, source hashes,

110
00:06:47,374 --> 00:06:51,745
rule outcomes, and recorded evidence provide traceability. The ebook includes

111
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:56,117
the data model and a join map to explain these

112
00:06:56,117 --> 00:06:56,554
relationships.

113
00:06:56,554 --> 00:07:01,463
Governance also needs accountable owners, access controls, retention decisions, and

114
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:06,373
an agreed response process. The private dashboard is documented as

115
00:07:06,373 --> 00:07:11,283
using workspace permissions. Production access and retention policies still require

116
00:07:11,283 --> 00:07:13,737
configuration in the deployment environment.

117
00:07:13,737 --> 00:07:18,156
The optional dbt layer adds documented SQL models, dependency lineage,

118
00:07:18,156 --> 00:07:22,575
and reusable tests. Its local validation is recorded separately from

119
00:07:22,575 --> 00:07:26,995
Databricks execution. The Azure DevOps file defines a proposed continuous

120
00:07:26,995 --> 00:07:31,414
integration workflow; it is not evidence that a live production

121
00:07:31,414 --> 00:07:33,181
deployment has already occurred.

122
00:07:33,181 --> 00:07:37,262
Before deployment, run regression tests and validate the rule changes.

123
00:07:37,262 --> 00:07:41,342
For scheduled processing, check changed inputs and use targeted queries

124
00:07:41,342 --> 00:07:45,422
where possible. Reserve full historical profiling for a periodic review

125
00:07:45,422 --> 00:07:49,502
or a material schema change. Route alerts to owners and

126
00:07:49,502 --> 00:07:53,582
suppress repeated unchanged alerts to reduce both compute cost and

127
00:07:53,582 --> 00:07:53,991
noise.

128
00:07:53,991 --> 00:07:58,127
AI assisted drafting and review, but its suggestions still needed

129
00:07:58,127 --> 00:08:02,264
testing. One rejected suggestion used a grouped first value to

130
00:08:02,264 --> 00:08:06,401
resolve conflicting payroll entries. That could silently select a salary

131
00:08:06,401 --> 00:08:10,538
and conceal an ambiguity. The chosen approach retains Cannot verify

132
00:08:10,538 --> 00:08:12,193
and preserves the evidence.

133
00:08:12,193 --> 00:08:15,528
The final review also corrected the local payroll status mapping.

134
00:08:15,528 --> 00:08:18,863
These examples show why a passing script is not enough:

135
00:08:18,863 --> 00:08:22,198
the business meaning of the test must be checked, and

136
00:08:22,198 --> 00:08:25,533
the test suite must challenge both valid and invalid cases.

137
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:29,221
To review the submission, extract the ZIP into a new

138
00:08:29,221 --> 00:08:32,909
folder and open Start Here. Read the ebook, inspect the

139
00:08:32,909 --> 00:08:36,596
dashboard captures, and compare the machine readable outputs with the

140
00:08:36,596 --> 00:08:40,284
code. Run the supplied local tests using the documented commands.

141
00:08:40,284 --> 00:08:43,603
The manifest provides a checksum for each packaged file.

142
00:08:43,603 --> 00:08:47,702
The remaining business action is to work with the source

143
00:08:47,702 --> 00:08:51,802
owners, correct confirmed defects in a controlled delivery, and rerun

144
00:08:51,802 --> 00:08:55,901
the controls. Only then should the release decision change. This

145
00:08:55,901 --> 00:09:00,000
concludes the walkthrough of the evidence, findings, implementation, and limitations.
